      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most likely causes for the irregular pressure spikes you're experiencing in your 2022 F-150's transmission are: 1) Faulty PCV valve or solenoid, 2) Clogged transmission cooler lines, or 3) Transmission pan gasket issue. These components can become clogged, allowing air to enter the hydraulic system, causing pressure spikes. Check your PCV system, transmission lines, and pan gasket for any blockages or leaks.",
